
MUSIC run for probe with protein.

The protein is a rigid solute and the probes are solvent 
molecules that only interact with the solute.

Many copies of the probe are made in a sphere of radius
cap-radius centered on cap-atom. MC/simulated annealing
is performed at three temperatures, T1, T2, and T3,
which are set in muscmd. They are currently 100, 0, -100 C.
2M MC configurations are sampled at T1 and T2, 1M at T3. 
The Lennard-Jones sigmas and epsilons for the solute atoms
can be scaled by SCLLJ, as also set in muscmd. 
SCLLJ = 0.85, 0.92, 1.00 at T1, T2, and T3 in the current muscmd.
You can play with these some, but if SCLLJ is too small, probe
atoms can get too close to protein atoms and cause problems
with starting the next temperature.

Execution time = 3-4 hours on a 2 GHz Pentium.

REQUIRED
(1) protein.z - z-matrix for protein. Protein is made rigid
and is not moved by removing all entries in protein.z after
the atom definitions. Several are in the proteins subdirectory.
Protein z-matrices are normally prepared with pepz in MCPRO.
If the protein is not rigid, it can get distorted to try to lower
the total interaction energy with all probe molecules.

(2) probe.z - z-matrix for the probe. This can be obtained by
xPROBE molecule
where molecule.z is the z-matrix for the probe in the
boss/molecules/small directory. It can include 800-899 atom types.
Otherwise, for any molecule.z
~/$BOSSdir/scripts/xSPM molecule
cp sum probe.z

(3) Edit muspar to set the cap-atom to the one for protein.z.
This will be the center of the probe sphere. You can change the
cap-radius, which controls the extent of the probe molecules.
There is a limit of 2500 probe molecules.

The limit for protein atoms is 4500 = MXAT.

EXECUTION
csh muscmd >& log &
will execute in the current directory

or

xMUSIC molecule >& log &
This gets molecule from boss/molecules/small and makes it the probe, and
runs MUSIC in the subdirectory molecule. The calling directory needs
to contain muscmd, muspar, and protein.z
e.g.,
xMUSIC benzen >& log &
performs the MUSIC run for benzene as the probe

A queue script could be written for this to perform multiple MUSIC
runs with different probes simultaneously.

muscmdshort is for short (5K) test jobs. It can be executed with, e.g.,
xSHORT benzen >& log &

MISCELLANEOUS
dmus is a RasMol script to help display the resulting plt files.
xNEAR can also be used to trim the system.
At the end of the output ot files, there is a listing of the interaction
energy for each probe molecule with the solute.

There are numerous probe possibilities -
benzen
meoh
chexan
pyrim
pyrid
isoxaz
oxazol
thiazl
phenol
nma
urea
...
see boss/molecules/small/INDEX


